# Root-lane counts for `-p delphi-runtime --tests`, ALL 17 targets under sudo.
#
# LANE RUN 15 — the round-26 remediation's first root execution. Measured 2026-09-06 at
# `0ad6556`.
#
#   EXECUTED 192 / SKIPPED 5 / reported 197     extractor rc=0
#   producers: 17/17 exited 0                   failures: 0
#   predicted 192/5/197 at 0ad6556, committed ALONE and BEFORE the run — and MATCHED EXACTLY
#
# WHAT THIS RUN ADDS OVER RUN 14: run 14's freshness check was real, but it ran BEFORE the
# round-26 remediation. Four security-relevant paths had never executed at root — the tier
# ceiling at `Confirm`, the deadline-bounded read, the `CLOCK_BOOTTIME` consent window, and the
# configurable read ceiling — plus the five tests that assert them. They have now.
#
# EVERY HYGIENE CHECK, WITH THE EVIDENCE THAT DECIDES IT (not merely that a step ran):
#
#   account          delphi-tool:x:997:972       (gid 972, not 997 — D0A-R17-02)
#   helper digest    aba0f0ea14b751aa…           INSTALLED == STAGED, both printed
#   bwrap            0.11.1
#   free space       /run 1484M, target 2297M, /tmp 3710M — all above floor, BUT SEE BELOW
#   forced freshness ENFORCED, not printed (D0A-R26-05). `sha256sum` over the enumerated set
#                    before and after `touch runtime/src/execute.rs` + rebuild; enumeration
#                    asserted at 17, BOTH hash sides asserted equal to 17, rebuild failure
#                    fatal, `diff` empty. Run 14's version printed the counts and compared
#                    anyway — a failed rebuild would have compared two stale sets and said
#                    FRESH. This one exits on each.
#   PAM before       439c1d1521d86e4eb011a927aff659db
#   PAM after        md5sum -c → OK              (class 16, the defect already paid for)
#   stale sessions   none, checked before AND after
#
# ⚠ FREE SPACE IS TRENDING DOWN AND IS THE THINNEST MARGIN IN THIS RECORD.
# `$CARGO_TARGET_DIR` read **4467M at run 14 and 2297M here — against a 2048M floor, i.e.
# 249M of headroom.** It passed; it is recorded because the next run may not, and because
# `/tmp` filling has already surfaced in this project as a BUILD error in an unrelated crate
# (see `scripts/check-free-space.sh`'s own rationale). A run that dies this way misattributes.
#
# THE FIVE SKIPS, each quoting its own blocker from the log — a skip proves nothing, so the
# list is read rather than the count:
#   b1_daemon_binary_runs_the_assembled_flow          needs --features insecure-test-seams
#   an_unreadable_login_defs_refuses_…                this uid can read a 0000 file
#   pidfd_refuses_a_recycled_pid_barrier              user namespaces unavailable here
#   live_logind_query_path_works_or_documents_…       standing DEFER (no logind session)
#   a_regular_login_user_is_not_refused_…             running as root
#
# THREE OF THE FIVE SKIP *BECAUSE* THE RUN IS PRIVILEGED and execute unprivileged. Root's 192
# and the unprivileged 172 are OVERLAPPING SETS, neither containing the other; "192 > 172" is
# not a coverage claim in either direction. Membership is read from the two skip LISTS, never
# computed from the two totals.
#
# BOTH LANES REPORT 197 — the consistency check committed in advance: same test set, different
# skip distribution. A different total would have meant the SET changed, a distinct defect from
# a count mismatch.
#
# THE TEST NAMED IN ADVANCE AS TIMING-TOLERANT DID NOT FAIL. The run-15 expectation flagged
# `boot_secs_reads_the_boottime_clock_and_does_not_go_backwards` — it tolerates a 1-second gap
# between two clock reads, the only one of the five that could fail for a reason unrelated to
# its property under a loaded serial run. Naming it in advance is what would have made a
# failure a diagnosis instead of a re-run.
#
# ORDERING HELD UNDER CONVENTION FOR THE THIRD CONSECUTIVE RUN (D0A-R22-01, still reopened).
# `0ad6556` contains the expectation file alone; the result follows. Three clean instances make
# the failure less likely, NOT the convention sufficient — nothing enforces it.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT A GREEN RUN 15 DOES **NOT** ESTABLISH — carried here because a residual recorded only
# beside the fix that created it gets read as part of that fix
#
# 1. THE SUSPEND DIVERGENCE IS UNMEASURED, NOT VERIFIED. R26-03 moved the consent window from
#    `Instant` (CLOCK_MONOTONIC, which PAUSES across suspend) to CLOCK_BOOTTIME. This box has
#    never suspended — BOOTTIME - MONOTONIC = 0.000s — so **no assertion available on this lane
#    distinguishes the two clocks.** The test that passed above checks clock IDENTITY. Do not
#    read this run as verifying the suspend behaviour; it cannot.
#
# 2. THE PENDING STORE HAS NO CAP. The read ceiling bounds ONE proposal at 2x; nothing bounds
#    accumulation across proposals. It sits ADJACENT to what R26-04 fixed — which got a
#    derivation, a config knob and a test — and that adjacency is exactly how it will be
#    mistaken for closed. Invisible while B1 services one action and exits; live when B2 loops.
#
# 3. `argv` IS EMPTINESS-CHECKED ONLY, while `env_delta` is NUL-checked at BOTH doors
#    (D0A-R18-03 / R19-05). Raised in the round-26 prompt; the findings did not answer it. A
#    question a reviewer declined to answer reads as settled unless it is recorded as
#    unanswered. It is UNANSWERED.
#
# Also: the read deadline's timeout branch is proven on a sleeping closure, not a stalled
# mount. That a real FUSE stall reaches it is a property of the filesystem, not of this code.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPERSEDED — LANE RUN 14 (`EXECUTED 187 / SKIPPED 5 / reported 192`, at `af6dde0`). Sound and
# not in doubt: it closed D0A-R24-01 with the first freshness check that actually hashed
# anything. Superseded only because it predates the round-26 remediation. Before it, run 13
# (`177/5/182`) whose freshness line was WITHDRAWN by D0A-R25-05, and runs 11/12 which split
# hygiene from counts.
EXECUTED=192
